1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:05,506
Welcome to Northwind. In the next three
minutes, you'll learn how to submit an

2
00:00:05,506 --> 00:00:08,414
expense claim that gets
paid the first time.

3
00:00:09,517 --> 00:00:14,068
Here's
why it matters. In twenty twenty-five, eighteen percent of expense claims

4
00:00:14,068 --> 00:00:16,685
were sent back, because
a receipt was missing.

5
00:00:16,685 --> 00:00:20,269
Claims with every receipt were
paid in about six business days.

6
00:00:21,383 --> 00:00:26,468
Four rules come before anything else.
Keep an itemised receipt for every expense

7
00:00:26,468 --> 00:00:30,473
over twenty-five dollars. A card
statement alone doesn't count.

8
00:00:30,473 --> 00:00:33,079
Submit within thirty days of the expense.

9
00:00:33,079 --> 00:00:35,940
After ninety days, a
claim isn't paid at all.

10
00:00:35,940 --> 00:00:40,199
And personal costs, like family
meals, are never business expenses.

11
00:00:41,283 --> 00:00:46,261
When you travel, these limits apply.
Meals are sixty dollars a day at home, and

12
00:00:46,261 --> 00:00:51,240
eighty-five dollars abroad. Hotels are
capped at two hundred and twenty dollars

13
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:55,336
a night, unless the Travel Desk
approves an exception in writing.

14
00:00:55,336 --> 00:00:59,873
Flights under six hours are economy.
And alcohol is only paid for client

15
00:00:59,873 --> 00:01:02,835
entertainment your manager
approved in advance.

16
00:01:03,950 --> 00:01:08,762
Now, the claim itself, in six steps.
Photograph the receipt on the same day.

17
00:01:08,762 --> 00:01:12,117
Open the Northwind Expenses
app and select New Claim.

18
00:01:12,117 --> 00:01:16,549
Choose the category, then enter the
date, amount and business purpose.

19
00:01:16,549 --> 00:01:20,285
Attach the receipt photo to
each line, and check the total.

20
00:01:20,285 --> 00:01:23,197
Submit it to your approver
within thirty days.

21
00:01:23,197 --> 00:01:27,566
And answer any question from your
approver within five business days.

22
00:01:28,650 --> 00:01:32,115
Who approves depends on
the amount. You submit.

23
00:01:32,115 --> 00:01:36,244
Your manager approves claims
up to one thousand dollars.

24
00:01:36,244 --> 00:01:41,995
A director approves up to five thousand.
And anything above five thousand goes

25
00:01:41,995 --> 00:01:42,954
to the C F O.

26
00:01:44,050 --> 00:01:48,647
Quick check. Your conference trip comes
to three thousand two hundred dollars.

27
00:01:48,647 --> 00:01:50,002
Who approves the claim?

28
00:01:52,202 --> 00:01:57,266
A director. It's above one thousand
dollars, but not above five thousand.

29
00:01:59,617 --> 00:02:04,240
Three things you must never do. Never
split one expense into several claims to

30
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:08,271
stay under a limit. Never submit
personal costs or private upgrades.

31
00:02:08,271 --> 00:02:12,953
And never inflate a claim. False claims
are treated as misconduct, and can lead

32
00:02:12,953 --> 00:02:17,577
to dismissal. Instead, submit each expense
once, with its real amount, and ask

33
00:02:17,577 --> 00:02:19,177
Finance when you're unsure.

34
00:02:20,283 --> 00:02:24,930
That's it. Keep the receipt, submit
within thirty days, and use the expense

35
00:02:24,930 --> 00:02:29,762
checklist in the next lesson. Questions?
Contact the Finance Help Desk through

36
00:02:29,762 --> 00:02:30,939
the service portal.
